## Autoregressive Generation Loop

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start(["User prompt\n'What is the capital of France?'"])
    
    Tok["Tokenize prompt\n→ integer IDs"]
    
    FP["Full forward pass\nAll N transformer layers\nEvery token attends to all prior tokens"]
    
    Sample["Sample next token\nsoftmax(logits / T)\n→ 'Paris'"]
    
    EOS{"Generated\nEOS token?"}
    
    Max{"Reached\nmax_tokens?"}
    
    Append["Append token to sequence\nnew_tokens = [prompt_tokens + 'Paris']"]
    
    Done(["Response complete\n'The capital of France is Paris.'"])

    Start --> Tok --> FP --> Sample --> EOS
    EOS -->|No| Max
    Max -->|No| Append --> FP
    EOS -->|Yes| Done
    Max -->|Yes| Done

    style Start fill:#EEEDFE,color:#3C3489
    style Done fill:#E1F5EE,color:#085041
    style Sample fill:#FAEEDA,color:#633806
    style EOS fill:#FAECE7,color:#4A1B0C
    style Max fill:#FAECE7,color:#4A1B0C
```

---

## KV Cache — Making Generation Fast

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph NoCa["❌ Without KV Cache"]
        direction TB
        T50["Token 50 arrives"]
        RC["Recompute K,V\nfor tokens 1 → 50\nO(n) work per step\nO(n²) total"]
    end
    
    subgraph Ca["✅ With KV Cache"]
        direction TB
        T50b["Token 50 arrives"]
        LC["Load cached K,V\nfor tokens 1 → 49\nfrom memory\n(no recomputation)"]
        NC["Compute K,V only\nfor token 50\nO(1) compute per step\nO(n) total"]
    end

    NoCa ~~~ Ca

    style RC fill:#FAECE7,color:#4A1B0C
    style LC fill:#E1F5EE,color:#085041
    style NC fill:#E1F5EE,color:#085041
```
